uvm_object_param_utils(T)

* 用于对有参数的object进行注册

```
// =========================================================================================== //
// When you use uvm_object_param_utils(my_param_object#(T)):                                   //
// The macro expands to uvm_object_param_utils_begin(my_param_object#(T)) followed by          //
// uvm_object_utils_end.                                                                       //
// The T in my_param_object#(T) is a placeholder for the actual type parameter that will be    //
// used when the class is instantiated.                                                        //
// The uvm_object_param_utils_begin(T) macro expands to:                                       //
//                                                                                             //
//    `m_uvm_object_registry_param(my_param_object#(T))                                        //
//    `m_uvm_object_create_func(my_param_object#(T))                                           //
//    `uvm_field_utils_begin(my_param_object#(T))                                              //
//                                                                                             //
// The key difference is in m_uvm_object_registry_param(T):                                    //
//                                                                                             //
//    typedef uvm_object_registry #(my_param_object#(T)) type_id;                              //
//                                                                                             //
// This creates a parameterized type_id for the class.                                         //
//                                                                                             //
// When you create a real type like my_param_object#(int) obj_int:                             //
// - The SystemVerilog compiler generates a specific version of the class where T is           //
//   replaced with int.                                                                        //
// - This includes generating a specific version of all the macros and functions defined       //
//   within the class.                                                                         //
//                                                                                             //
// The factory registration process:                                                           //
// - When get_type() is called (usually during construction or registration), it calls         //
//   type_id::get().                                                                           //
// - type_id::get() creates a new uvm_object_registry instance specific to                     //
//   my_param_object#(int).                                                                    //
// - This instance is registered with the factory.                                             //
// - The factory now has a unique entry for my_param_object#(int):                             //
//   - It's different from entries for my_param_object#(byte), my_param_object#(shortint), etc.//
// - Each parameterized version of the class gets its own unique factory registration.         //
//                                                                                             //
// Creating objects:                                                                           //
// - When you call my_param_object#(int)::type_id::create("obj_int"), the factory knows        //
//   exactly which version of the class to instantiate.                                        //
//                                                                                             //
// Important note:                                                                             //
// - The uvm_object_param_utils macro doesn't directly handle the parameter substitution.      //
// - The substitution is handled by the SystemVerilog compiler when you actually use the       //
//   parameterized class with a specific type.                                                 //
//                                                                                             //
// In summary, uvm_object_param_utils sets up the class to work with the UVM factory system    //
// in a way that's compatible with parameterized classes. The actual type substitution         //
// happens when you use the class with specific parameters, and the UVM factory system is      //
// designed to work with these parameterized types, creating unique registrations for each     //
// parameter combination.                                                                      //
// =========================================================================================== //

// ================================================================================================= //
// Let's consider an example where we mistakenly use uvm_object_utils to register a parameterized    //
// class instead of using uvm_object_param_utils. Here's an example and analysis:                    //
//                                                                                                   //
// class my_parameterized_class #(type T = int) extends uvm_object;                                  //
//   T data;                                                                                         //
//                                                                                                   //
//   function new(string name = "my_parameterized_class");                                           //
//     super.new(name);                                                                              //
//   endfunction                                                                                     //
//                                                                                                   //
/

