compose_report_message

* 被 [process_report_message]() 调用，将所有message信息获取并组建成一个字符串返回，用户可以自定义server并重写这个函数
* 这个方法中实现了当前仿真时间的获取，可以看到这个时间是通过$time（注意：这里与UVM-1.1不同）获取的，而$time获取的时间是一个整型数据，并且此时显示的时间也受$timeformat设置的默认值的影响，即此时显示的时间单位是该语句执行时所在域的时间精度，所以此时我们看到`uvm_info调用时在log中显示的时间是一个五位数并且只保留了对应时间单位的整数部分数字，显示的时间就与波形上期望的小数存在了较大的差异，此时**虽然可以通过$timeformat进行设置，但是也不会获得时间精度对应的具体小数部分的数字了**。

* Responsible for creating a formatted string representation of a UVM report message. Here's a summary of its key features:

  - **Purpose**: Composes a detailed, formatted string from a uvm_report_message object.
  - **Input**: Takes a uvm_report_message object and an optional report_object_name string.
  - **Output**: Returns a single string containing all relevant message information.
  - **Composition elements**:
    - Severity level (e.g., UVM_INFO, UVM_ERROR)
    - Verbosity level (if enabled)
    - File name and line number (if available)
    - Simulation time (using $time)
    - Context string (if available)
    - Report object name
    - Message ID
    - Message body
    - Additional message elements (if any)
    - Terminator string (if enabled)
  - **Flexibility**:
    - Handles optional elements like verbosity and terminator strings
    - Accommodates additional message elements through uvm_report_message_element_container
  - **Time representation**: Uses $time, which may not provide sub-unit precision.
  - **Customization**: Can be overridden in custom report servers to modify message formatting.

```systemverilog
  virtual function string compose_report_message(uvm_report_message report_message,
                                                 string report_object_name = "");

    // Declare variables for composing the message
    string sev_string;
    uvm_severity l_severity;
    uvm_verbosity l_verbosity;
    string filename_line_string;
    string time_str;
    string line_str;
    string context_str;
    string verbosity_str;
    string terminator_str;
    string msg_body_str;
    uvm_report_message_element_container el_container;
    string prefix;
    uvm_report_handler l_report_handler;

    // Get the severity of the report message
    l_severity = report_message.get_severity();
    sev_string = l_severity.name();

    // Compose filename and line number string if available
    if (report_message.get_filename() != "") begin
      line_str.itoa(report_message.get_line());
      filename_line_string = {report_message.get_filename(), "(", line_str, ") "};
    end

    // Get current simulation time
    // Note: This uses $time, which may not provide sub-unit precision
    $swrite(time_str, "%0t", $time);

    // Add context string if available
    if (report_message.get_context() != "")
      context_str = {"@@", report_message.get_context()};

    // Add verbosity information if enabled
    if (show_verbosity) begin
      if ($cast(l_verbosity, report_message.get_verbosity()))
        verbosity_str = l_verbosity.name();
      else
        verbosity_str.itoa(report_message.get_verbosity());
      verbosity_str = {"(", verbosity_str, ")"};
    end

    // Add terminator string if enabled
    if (show_terminator)
      terminator_str = {" -",sev_string};

    // Compose message body, including any additional elements
    el_container = report_message.get_element_container();
    if (el_container.size() == 0)
      msg_body_str = report_message.get_message();
    else begin
      prefix = uvm_default_printer.knobs.prefix;
      uvm_default_printer.knobs.prefix = " +";
      msg_body_str = {report_message.get_message(), "\n", el_container.sprint()};
      uvm_default_printer.knobs.prefix = prefix;
    end

    // Get report object name
    if (report_object_name == "") begin
      l_report_handler = report_message.get_report_handler();
      report_object_name = l_report_handler.get_full_name();
    end

    // Compose the final report message
    compose_report_message = {sev_string, verbosity_str, " ", filename_line_string, "@ ", 
      time_str, ": ", report_object_name, context_str,
      " [", report_message.get_id(), "] ", msg_body_str, terminator_str};

  endfunction 
```

