m_do_cycle_check

```systemverilog
bit             cycle_check[uvm_object];

uvm_object m_uvm_cycle_scopes[$];
function bit m_do_cycle_check(uvm_object scope);
  uvm_object l = (m_uvm_cycle_scopes.size()==0) ? null : m_uvm_cycle_scopes[$];

  // we have been in this scope before (but actually right before so assuming a super/derived context of the same object)
  if(l == scope) 
  begin
     m_uvm_cycle_scopes.push_back(scope);
     return 0;
  end
  else
  begin
      // now check if we have already been in this scope before
      uvm_object m[$] = m_uvm_cycle_scopes.find_first(item) with (item == scope);
      if(m.size()!=0) begin
           return 1;   //   detected a cycle 
      end
      else begin
          m_uvm_cycle_scopes.push_back(scope);
          return 0;            
      end
  end
endfunction
```

uvm_comparer

* Provides methods for comparing various types of data, including integers, real numbers, objects, and strings.
* uvm_comparer 类是一个专用于比较数据的类，它的主体是 compare_field，compare_field_int，compare_field_real，compare_object,  compare_string，分别用于比较整数，整数，实数，类，字符串

  <img width="800" alt="image" src="https://github.com/jiru1997/VLSI-Design-verification-interview/assets/66343787/cd78ae4c-67bc-4068-8eb8-2aabb6b446aa">

* 这里使用了一个 [uvm_object_globals:uvm_recursion_policy_enum]() 类型的变量 policy

```systemverilog
class uvm_comparer;

  // Determines whether comparison is UVM_DEEP, UVM_REFERENCE, or UVM_SHALLOW.
  uvm_recursion_policy_enum policy        = UVM_DEFAULT_POLICY;

  // Sets the maximum number of messages to send to the printer for miscompares
  int unsigned              show_max      = 1;

  // The verbosity setting is used by the messaging mechanism to determine
  int unsigned              verbosity     = UVM_LOW;

  // The severity setting is used by the messaging mechanism for printing and
  uvm_severity              sev           = UVM_INFO;

  // The string holds the last set of miscompares that occurred during a
  // comparison.
  string                    miscompares   = "";

  // The abstract and physical settings allow an object to distinguish between
  // two different classes of fields.
  bit                       physical      = 1;

  // The abstract and physical settings allow an object to distinguish between
  // two different classes of fields.
  bit                       abstract      = 1;

  // This bit determines whether the type, given by <uvm_object::get_type_name>,
  // is used to verify that the types of two objects are the same. 
  bit                       check_type    = 1;

  // This bit stores the number of miscompares for a given compare operation.
  // You can use the result to determine the number of miscompares that
  // were found.
  int unsigned              result        = 0;

  int                       depth;          // Current depth of objects
  uvm_object                compare_map[uvm_object];
  uvm_scope_stack           scope         = new;
```

| Feature | compare_field | compare_field_int | compare_field_real | compare_object | compare_string |
|---------|---------------|-------------------|---------------------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Data Type | uvm_bitstream_t | uvm_integral_t | real | uvm_object | string |
| Max Size | 4096 bits | 64 bits | N/A | N/A | N/A |
| Comparison Method | Bitwise AND with mask | Bitwise AND with mask | Direct comparison (!=) | Reference or deep comparison | Direct comparison (!=) |
| Radix Support | Yes (BIN, OCT, DEC, HEX, etc.) | Yes (BIN, OCT, DEC, HEX, etc.) | No | No | No |
| Null Handling | N/A | N/A | N/A | Yes | N/A |
| Recursion Policy | N/A | N/A | N/A | Yes (UVM_REFERENCE, UVM_DEEP) | N/A |
| Scope Tracking | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Delegate to Other Methods | Yes (to compare_field_int for ≤64 bits) | No | No | Yes (to object's compare method) | No |
| Mismatch Reporting | Via print_msg | Via print_msg | Via print_msg | Via print_msg_object | Via print_msg |
| Return Value | bit (1 for match, 0 for mismatch) | bit (1 for match, 0 for mismatch) | bit (1 for match, 0 for mismatch) | bit (1 for match, 0 for mismatch) | bit (1 for match, 0 for mismatch) |

* Key differences:

1. Comparison method:
   - compare_field and compare_field_int use masking
   - Others use direct comparison

2. Radix support:
   - Only compare_field and compare_field_int support different radix formats for mismatch reporting

3. Complexity:
   - compare_object is the most complex
     - Handles null cases
     - Supports different recursion policies

4. Bit size handling:
   - compare_field can handle larger bit sizes compared to compare_field_int

5. Deep comparison:
   - compare_object is the only method that potentially calls another object's compare method for deep comparison

6. Simplicity:
   - compare_field_real and compare_string are the simplest
   - Perform direct value comparisons



