pack_bits

* pack data in big endian mode

  <img width="550" alt="image" src="https://github.com/jiru1997/VLSI-Design-verification-interview/assets/66343787/9929646f-3233-4309-b02d-5ab79a616a28">

* Purpose: Pack arrays of bits, bytes, or integers.
* Operation: Stores data in m_bits, handling size checks and endianness.
* Key feature: Efficient packing of array data.

```systemverilog
function void uvm_packer::pack_bits(ref bit value[], input int size = -1);
   if (size < 0)
     size = value.size();

   if (size > value.size()) begin
      `uvm_error("UVM/BASE/PACKER/BAD_SIZE",
                 $sformatf("pack_bits called with size '%0d', which exceeds value.size() of '%0d'",
                           size,
                           value.size()))
      return;
   end

   for (int i=0; i<size; i++)
     if (big_endian == 1)
       m_bits[count+i] = value[size-1-i];
     else
       m_bits[count+i] = value[i];
